{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"btvqkdxk6","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vgq6HvG5U1tATdJpAxPre1","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run1-repo/b0932c02-74bc-4693-b4ae-4a322798211e/tasks/btvqkdxk6.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_0\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nPeople keep a running tally of heads versus tails as they read a sequence and expect a fair coin to keep correcting itself: the tally should drift away from balance and then come back to even, again and again. A sequence whose tally returns to an even count often (relative to how many returns its length allows) looks self-correcting and so more random, while one whose tally wanders off and rarely or never comes back to balance looks biased — by a shared weight on the share of possible returns to balance, on top of the current best judgement (personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity with lenience toward over-alternation, personal weights on imbalance and the longest streak, a personal pattern-detection gain scaling the final streak, mirror symmetry, complement symmetry, run-length variety and most-lopsided-stretch cues, and a personal guessing rate). It predicts that two sequences with the same final counts, switching rate and range of the tally differ when one passes through balance more often along the way (HTTHHT versus HHTTTH... e.g. THHTHT beats HHTTHT less often than HTTHTH does).\nEOF\necho returns_to_balance_expectation > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc=open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/personal_pattern_detection_gain.py\").read()\ndoc_end=src.index('\"\"\"',3)+3\nsrc='''\"\"\"Returns-to-balance expectation.\n\nPeople keep a running tally of heads versus tails while reading a sequence and\nexpect a fair coin to keep correcting itself, the tally returning to an even\ncount again and again. A sequence whose tally returns to balance often (as a\nshare of the returns its length allows) looks more random, by a shared weight,\non top of the current best judgement (personal ideal switching rate and\nsensitivity with asymmetric tolerance, personal weights on imbalance and the\nlongest run, a personal pattern-detection gain scaling the structural cues,\nand a personal lapse rate).\n\"\"\"'''+src[doc_end:]\nsrc=src.replace('''    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''','''    def balance_returns(seq):\n        # Share of the possible returns of the running tally to an even count.\n        tally, returns = 0, 0\n        for x in seq:\n            tally += 1 if x == \"H\" else -1\n            if tally == 0:\n                returns += 1\n        return returns / (len(seq) // 2)\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        \"antisym_b\": complement_symmetric(b),\n    }''','''        \"antisym_b\": complement_symmetric(b),\n        \"returns_a\": balance_returns(a),\n        \"returns_b\": balance_returns(b),\n    }''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    participant_id = pm.Data(''','''    returns_a = pm.Data(\"returns_a\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    returns_b = pm.Data(\"returns_b\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    participant_id = pm.Data(''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    # Personal pattern-detection gain''','''    # Shared weight on returns of the tally to balance (positive: self-correcting looks random).\n    tau = pm.Normal(\"tau\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)\n\n    # Personal pattern-detection gain''')\nsrc=src.replace(\"lopsided_a, antisym_a)\\n\",\"lopsided_a, antisym_a) + tau * returns_a\\n\")\nsrc=src.replace(\"lopsided_b, antisym_b)\\n\",\"lopsided_b, antisym_b) + tau * returns_b\\n\")\nassert src.count(\"tau * returns\")==2\nopen(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_0/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"1eb70cf2-a172-424f-92f1-8cd32e2dc397","session_id":"b0932c02-74bc-4693-b4ae-4a322798211e"}
